<h3 id="contactsjson">contacts.json</h3>
<div class="tablewrap"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Field</th>
<th>Type</th>
<th>Meaning</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>contacts</code></td>
<td>array, at most 1016</td>
<td>The address book, in callsign order (APRS-37).</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>contacts[].call</code></td>
<td>string</td>
<td>3-9 characters: <code>A-Z</code>, <code>0-9</code>, <code>-</code> (<code>VE7ABC-9</code>).</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>contacts[].name</code></td>
<td>string</td>
<td>Up to 12 characters: letters, digits, space and <code>- . / _ # + &amp; ( ) ' !</code>. Others become <code>-</code>.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p>Contacts aren't one record: Console writes them by callsign. Opening a file adds or renames those contacts on Write;
it deletes none.</p>
<h3 id="quickjson">quick.json</h3>
<div class="tablewrap"><table>
